# EB ships ONLY what the API needs — not the Expo app.
# Important: EB writes .ebignore-based zip of the repo; these rules pare it down.
*
!.gitignore
!Procfile
!.platform/
!.platform/**/*
# CRITICAL: ship the EB hooks that npm-install the server deps on the instance.
# Without this the deployed env has NO node_modules and the web process can't
# start ("Cannot find module 'dotenv/config'").
!.ebextensions/
!.ebextensions/**/*
!server/
!server/**/*
!server/node_modules/*
server/node_modules/.cache/
# Never ship platform-specific native binaries. server/node_modules is built on the
# developer's machine, so a Windows checkout would otherwise deliver
# @img/sharp-win32-x64 to a Linux instance. sharp is only ever loaded lazily, so
# nothing fails until the first vehicle photo is fetched - which is exactly how every
# car ended up with no image while CarsXE happily returned 9 of them. The .platform
# hooks install the correct build for the instance.
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-win32-x64/
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-wasm32/
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-darwin-x64/
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-darwin-arm64/
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-linux-arm/
server/node_modules/@img/sharp-linux-arm64/